    {
      "id": "3552vay",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Types of Protected Areas in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Protected areas in India are categorized primarily into National Parks, Wildlife Sanctuaries, Community Reserves, and Conservation Reserves under the Wildlife Protection Act, 1972.",
        "National Parks provide the highest degree of protection where no human activity, grazing, or forestry is permitted.",
        "Wildlife Sanctuaries allow limited human activities such as resource collection and regulated grazing.",
        "Major government conservation initiatives include Project Tiger (1973) and Project Elephant (1992) to protect critical species and their ecosystems."
      ],
      "id": "rspzooq"
    },
